 1st District pairs incumbent Democrat Frank Mrvan against Republican Barb Regnitz, who won a Trump endorsement in July and has drawn national GOP resources into the race. The seat carries only a slight Democratic lean, making it one of Indiana's more competitive House districts on paper.\n\nStill, the evidence favors Mrvan. Every major race rater places the contest at Likely D or safer, and prediction markets give him roughly a 96-98% chance of reelection. Fundraising is essentially even, with Mrvan holding a modest cash edge and benefiting from outside support. The forecast expects a Democratic win in the high single digits to low double digits, with enough uncertainty to keep the race out of the safe column given the absence of local polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9569, "margin": 11.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9243, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9308, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9246, "margin": 10.6}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9079, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9227, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9206, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9443, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.938, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9373, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9482, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9254, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9274, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9315, "margin": 10.5}]}